flowchart TD
A[HR submits salary revision] --> B[Validate salary, date and reason]
B --> C{Input valid?}
C -->|No| D[Return validation errors]
C -->|Yes| E[Load employee and salary history]
E --> F{Employee exists?}
F -->|No| G[Return not found]
F -->|Yes| H{Create or edit upcoming revision?}

H -->|Create| I[Check upcoming revision count]
I --> J{Less than 2 upcoming?}
J -->|No| K[Reject creation]
J -->|Yes| L[Check effective date conflict]

L --> M{Date already exists?}
M -->|Yes| N[Reject duplicate date]
M -->|No| O[Begin transaction and insert revision]

H -->|Edit| P[Load existing revision]
P --> Q{Revision is upcoming?}
Q -->|No| R[Reject edit]
Q -->|Yes| S[Validate updated effective date]
S --> T{Date is today or later?}
T -->|No| U[Reject edit]
T -->|Yes| V[Check date conflict]
V --> W{Conflict with another revision?}
W -->|Yes| X[Reject edit]
W -->|No| Y[Begin transaction and update existing revision]

O --> Z{Effective date is today?}
Y --> Z
Z -->|Yes| AA[Update employee current salary]
Z -->|No| AB[Leave current salary unchanged]
AA --> AC[Commit transaction]
AB --> AC
AC --> AD[Return success]

O -->|Failure| AE[Rollback]
Y -->|Failure| AE

subgraph Employee Creation
BA[HR submits employee details and initial salary] --> BB[Validate fields]
BB --> BC[Begin transaction]
BC --> BD[Insert employee]
BD --> BE[Insert initial salary history using joining date]
BE --> BF{Both writes successful?}
BF -->|No| BG[Rollback transaction]
BF -->|Yes| BH[Commit transaction]
end

subgraph Upcoming Revisions
BI[Load salary history] --> BJ[Identify upcoming revisions by effective date]
BJ --> BK[Sort revisions by effective date]
BK --> BL[Display upcoming revisions in HR interface]
end
